 "drug_rule": "Caffeine and doxepin have opposing central nervous system effects. Caffeine blocks adenosine receptors, promoting wakefulness, while doxepin enhances GABA-A activity and blocks histamine H1 receptors, producing sedation. Co-administration can reduce sleep quality and may increase the risk of daytime sedation or paradoxical CNS stimulation.",
